#region - Communication Note

Function Get-AutomateNOWCommunicationNote {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Searches for Communication Notes related to the provided object within an instance of AutomateNOW! Explicit filters are combined with the object scope and existing reply/archive filters using AND. SubjectType and SourceType use equals with arrays of enum labels.

    .DESCRIPTION
    Searches for Communication Notes related to the provided object within an instance of AutomateNOW! Explicit filters are combined with the object scope and existing reply/archive filters using AND. SubjectType and SourceType use equals with arrays of enum labels.

    .PARAMETER NoteType
    Optional string to filter the results by the type of Communication Note. Valid choices are: INFO, WARNING, QUESTION, CHANGE_REQUEST and PROBLEM

    .PARAMETER Status
    Optional string to filter the results by the status of the Communication Notes. Valid choices are: NEW, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED and CLOSED

    .PARAMETER SubjectType
    Optional enum array to filter the results by the subject type of the Communication Notes. Valid choices are: PROCESSING, PROCESSING_TEMPLATE, SERVER_NODE, AGENT, ENDPOINT and RESOURCE

    .PARAMETER SourceName
    Optional case-sensitive string to filter the results by the name of the source of the Communication Note. This is typically the name of a user.

    .PARAMETER SourceType
    Optional enum array to filter the results by the source type of the Communication Notes. Valid choices are: USER, PROCESSING, SERVER_NODE, AGENT and RESOURCE

    .PARAMETER SubjectName
    Optional literal string to filter the results exactly by the "name" of the subject of the Communication Note. This will either be the simple id of a design object or the numerical id of a processing object (i.e. A Task or Workflow). See the examples.

    .PARAMETER SubjectId
    Optional literal string to filter the results exactly by the "id" of the subject of the Communication Note. This will either be the full id of a design object or the numerical id of a processing object (i.e. A Task or Workflow). See the examples.

    .PARAMETER Id
    String parameter containing the specific Id of the Communication Note to fetch. This is a 36-character GUID. You may not combine this parameter with other parameters (except -Conversation)

    .PARAMETER Conversation
    Switch parameter that will return all of the replies to the Note specified by the -Id parameter. This parameter requires the -Id parameter.

    .PARAMETER sortBy
    Optional string parameter to sort the results by (may not be used with the Id parameter). Valid choices are: dateCreated*, noteSubjectName, noteSubjectId, noteStatus, noteSubjectCategory, content, noteSourceType, noteSourceName, noteSourceId, noteSubjectType, id

    .PARAMETER Ascending
    Optional switch parameter to sort in ascending order

    .PARAMETER startRow
    An optional int32 representing what row to start the download from. The default is 0.

    .PARAMETER endRow
    An optional int32 representing how many rows of data to receive. The default is 100.

    .PARAMETER TaskTemplate
    [ANOWTaskTemplate] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWTaskTemplate to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER WorkflowTemplate
    [ANOWWorkflowTemplate] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWWorkflowTemplate to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerTemplate
    [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER ScheduleTemplate
    [ANOWScheduleTemplate] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWScheduleTemplate to obtain these objects. Note: The console refers to these as 'Schedules'.

    .PARAMETER Task
    [ANOWTask] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWTask to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Workflow
    [ANOWWorkflow] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWWorkflow to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER ServiceManager
    [ANOWServiceManager] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Schedule
    [ANOWSchedule] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWSchedule to obtain these objects. Note: The console refers to these as 'Schedules'.

    .PARAMETER Agent
    [ANOWAgent] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWAgent to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER ServerNode
    [ANOWServerNode] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWServerNode to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Endpoint
    [ANOWEndpoint] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWEndpoint to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Stock
    [ANOWStock] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWStock to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Lock
    [ANOWLock] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWLock to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Semaphore
    [ANOWSemaphore] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWSemaphore to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER TimeWindow
    [ANOWTimeWindow] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWTimeWindow to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Variable
    [ANOWVariable] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWVariable to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER PhysicalResource
    [ANOWPhysicalResource] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWPhysicalResource to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Metric
    [ANOWMetric] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWMetric to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Event
    [ANOWEvent] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWEvent to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Calendar
    [ANOWCalendar] object to search for Communicate Notes against. Use Get-AutomateNOWCalendar to obtain these objects.

    .INPUTS
    Accepts the following types of ANOW objects: Agent, Calendar, Endpoint, Event, Lock, Metric, PhysicalResource, Schedule, ScheduleTemplate, Semaphore, ServerNode, ServiceManager, ServiceManagerTemplate, Stock, Task, TaskTemplate, TimeWindow, Variable, Workflow, WorkflowTemplate

    .OUTPUTS
    The related [ANOWCommunicationNote] objects (if any) will be returned.

    .EXAMPLE
    Gets a single Communication Note by Id

    Get-AutomateNOWCommunicationNote -Id '2b509023-372f-47a9-9a34-135c83239a34'

    .EXAMPLE
    Gets the first page of replies to a specific note by its Id

    Get-AutomateNOWCommunicationNote -Id 'ead543dc-e68c-4db2-a2d2-be283a189f87' -Conversation

    .EXAMPLE
