    An int32 representing the number of scheduled items to preload in advance. By default the type of preload is "persistent". According to the documentation: This means loading a specific number of items in advance, before the scheduled time, so they’re ready for future use.

    .PARAMETER Adhoc
    A switch parameter which represents the 'Adhoc Preload'. According to the documentation: This refers to loading a set number of items just once, for a one-time use. Future instances of this item will be loaded into the active queue ahead of the scheduled execution time.

    .PARAMETER Force
    Force the change without confirmation. This is equivalent to -Confirm:$false

    .PARAMETER Quiet
    Switch parameter to silence the emitted informational message.

    .INPUTS
    ONLY [ANOWScheduleTemplate] objects are accepted (including from the pipeline)

    .OUTPUTS
    An information message will be written to the console.

    .EXAMPLE
    Preloads (persistent mode) the first scheduled item for a Schedule Template named 'ScheduleTemplate1'

    Get-AutomateNOWScheduleTemplate -Id 'ScheduleTemplate1' | Import-AutomateNOWScheduleTemplate -PreloadCounter 1

    .EXAMPLE
    Forcibly and quietly preloads (adhoc mode) the first scheduled item for a Schedule Template named 'ScheduleTemplate1'

    Get-AutomateNOWScheduleTemplate -Id 'ScheduleTemplate1' | Import-AutomateNOWScheduleTemplate -PreloadCounter 1 -Adhoc -Force -Quiet

    .NOTES
