    Force Completes or Force Fails a Service Manager on an AutomateNOW! instance

    .DESCRIPTION
    Force Completes or Force Fails a Service Manager on an AutomateNOW! instance

    .PARAMETER ServiceManager
    An [ANOWServiceManager] object representing the Service Manager to be completed

    .PARAMETER ForceFail
    Switch parameter that alters this function set 'Force Failed' instead of 'Force Completed'

    .PARAMETER KeepForcedStatus
    Optional switch parameter that keeps the 'Forced' status after the Agent updates.

    .PARAMETER ForbidChildrenStart
    Optional switch parameter that disallows child items from starting

    .PARAMETER AbortChildren
    Optional switch parameter that softly aborts executing items within the Service Manager

    .PARAMETER KillChildren
    Optional switch parameter that hard kills executing items within the Service Manager

    .PARAMETER ForceChildren
    Optional switch parameter that recursively force completes child items

    .PARAMETER Force
    Force the restart without confirmation. This is equivalent to -Confirm:$false

    .PARAMETER Quiet
    Switch parameter to suppress the informational message and the Force Completed Service Manager

    .INPUTS
    ONLY [ANOWServiceManager] objects are accepted (including from the pipeline)

    .OUTPUTS
    The updated [ANOWServiceManager] object is returned unless -Quiet is used

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Completes a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Allow children processing | Restate status on child status change
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Completes a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Allow children processing | Keep completed status on child status change
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -KeepForcedStatus

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Completes a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Disallow children processing | Disallow start but allow executing items to complete
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Completes a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Disallow children processing | Disallow start and softly abort executing items
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart -abortChildren

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Completes a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Disallow children processing | Disallow start and hard kill executing items
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart -KillChildren

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Completes a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Recursively force complete child items
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -ForceChildren

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Fails a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Allow children processing | Restate status on child status change
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -ForceFail

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Fails a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Allow children processing | Keep completed status on child status change
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -ForceFail -KeepForcedStatus

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Fails a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Disallow children processing | Disallow start but allow executing items to complete
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -ForceFail -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Fails a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Disallow children processing | Disallow start and softly abort executing items
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -ForceFail -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart -abortChildren

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Fails a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. Disallow children processing | Disallow start and hard kill executing items
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -ForceFail -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart -KillChildren

    .EXAMPLE
    Force Fails a Service Manager with a (Run) Id of 123456. This is the equivalent to: Recursively force complete child items
    123456 | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager | Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager -ForceFail -ForceChildren

    .NOTES
    You must use Connect-AutomateNOW to establish the token by way of global variable.

    Use the below table to achieve the equivalent effect from the UI:

    Allow children processing | Keep completed status on child status change            | -KeepForcedStatus
    Allow children processing | Restate status on child status change                   | (no parameters)
    Disallow children processing | Disallow start but allow executing items to complete | -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart
    Disallow children processing | Disallow start and softly abort executing items      | -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart -AbortChildren
    Disallow children processing | Disallow start and hard kill executing items         | -KeepForcedStatus -ForbidChildrenStart -KillChildren
    Recursively force complete child items                                              | -ForceChildren

    #>
    [OutputType([ANOWServiceManager])]
    [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess, DefaultParameterSetName = 'Default', ConfirmImpact = 'High')]
    Param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ValueFromPipeline = $True)]
        [ANOWServiceManager]$ServiceManager,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$ForceFail,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'KeepForcedStatus')]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'ForbidChildrenStart')]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'abortChildren')]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'killChildren')]
        [switch]$KeepForcedStatus,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'ForbidChildrenStart')]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'abortChildren')]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'killChildren')]
        [switch]$ForbidChildrenStart,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'abortChildren')]
        [switch]$AbortChildren,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'killChildren')]
        [switch]$KillChildren,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'ForceChildren')]
        [switch]$ForceChildren,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Force,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Quiet
    )
    Begin {
        If ((Confirm-AutomateNOWSession -Quiet) -ne $true) {
            Write-Warning -Message "There is not a valid token confirmed."
            Break
        }
        If ($ForceFail -ne $true) {
            [string]$command = '/processing/forceCompleted'
            [string]$operationId = 'forceCompleted'
            [string]$action = 'Force Completed'
        }
        Else {
            [string]$command = '/processing/forceFailed'
            [string]$operationId = 'forceFailed'
            [string]$action = 'Force Failed'
        }
        [hashtable]$parameters = @{}
        $parameters.Add('Command', $command)
        $parameters.Add('Method', 'POST')
        $parameters.Add('ContentType', 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=UTF-8')
        If ($anow_session.NotSecure -eq $true) {
            $parameters.Add('NotSecure', $true)
        }
    }
    Process {
        If ($_ -is [ANOWServiceManager]) {
            [ANOWServiceManager]$ServiceManager = $_
        }
        [int64]$ServiceManager_id = $ServiceManager.id
        [string]$current_service_manager_status = $ServiceManager.processingStatus
        If (($current_service_manager_status -eq 'FAILED') -and ($operationId -eq 'forceFailed')) {
            Write-Warning -Message "You cannot Force Fail an already failed Service Manager"
            Break
        }
        ElseIf (($current_service_manager_status -eq 'COMPLETED') -and ($operationId -eq 'forceCompleted')) {
            Write-Warning -Message "You cannot Force Complete an already completed Service Manager"
            Break
        }
        If (($Force -eq $true -and -not $WhatIfPreference) -or ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess("$($ServiceManager_id)")) -eq $true) {
            ## Begin warning ##
            ## Do not tamper with this below code which makes sure that the object exists before attempting to change it.
            $Error.Clear()
            Try {
                [ANOWServiceManager]$current_service_manager = Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager -Id $ServiceManager_id
            }
            Catch {
                [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
                Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager failed to check if the Service Manager [$ServiceManager_id] existed under Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager due to [$Message]."
                Break
            }
            If ($current_service_manager.id -eq 0) {
                Write-Warning -Message "The Service Manager you specified does not seem to exist under Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager"
                Break
            }
            [string]$current_service_manager_status = $current_service_manager.processingStatus
            If ($current_service_manager_status -notin [ANOWProcessing_processingStatus].GetEnumNames()) {
                Write-Warning -Message "The processing status of the Service Manager [$ServiceManager_id] cannot be read under Complete-AutomateNOWServiceManager"
                Break
            }
            ## End warning ##
            [System.Collections.Specialized.OrderedDictionary]$BodyMetaData = [System.Collections.Specialized.OrderedDictionary]@{}
            If ($KeepForcedStatus -eq $true) {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('keepForcedStatus', 'true')
            }
            Else {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('keepForcedStatus', 'false')
            }
            If ($ForbidChildrenStart -eq $true) {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('forbidChildrenStart', 'true')
            }
            Else {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('forbidChildrenStart', 'false')
            }
            If ($KillChildren -eq $true) {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('killChildren', 'true')
            }
            Else {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('killChildren', 'false')
            }
            If ($AbortChildren -eq $true) {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('abortChildren', 'true')
            }
            Else {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('abortChildren', 'false')
            }
            If ($ForceChildren -eq $true) {
                $BodyMetaData.Add('forceChildren', 'true')
            }
            $BodyMetaData.Add('id', $ServiceManager_id )
            $BodyMetaData.Add('_operationType', 'custom')
            $BodyMetaData.Add('_operationId', $operationId)
            $BodyMetaData.Add('_textMatchStyle', 'exact')
            $BodyMetaData.Add('_dataSource', 'ProcessingDataSource')
            $BodyMetaData.Add('isc_metaDataPrefix', '_')
            $BodyMetaData.Add('isc_dataFormat', 'json')
            [string]$Body = ConvertTo-QueryString -InputObject $BodyMetaData
            If ($null -eq $parameters.Body) {
                $parameters.Add('Body', $Body)
            }
            Else {
                $parameters.Body = $Body
            }
            $Error.Clear()
            Try {
                [PSCustomObject]$results = Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI @parameters
            }
            Catch {
                [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
                Write-Warning -Message "Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI failed to execute [$command] on [$ServiceManager_id] due to [$Message]."
                Break
            }
            [int32]$response_code = $results.response.status
            If ($response_code -ne 0) {
                [string]$full_response_display = $results.response | ConvertTo-Json -Compress -Depth 100
                Write-Warning -Message "The response code was not 0 but was [$response_code]. Body: $full_response_display"
                Break
            }
            If ($Quiet -ne $true) {
                $Error.Clear()
                Try {
                    [ANOWServiceManager]$completed_service_manager = Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager -Id $ServiceManager_id
                }
                Catch {
                    Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWServiceManager failed to retrieve the Service Manager (after it was already '$action') due to [$Message]"
                    Break
                }
                Return $completed_service_manager
            }
        }
    }
    End {

    }
}

#endregion

#region - Service Manager Template (PROCESSING_TEMPLATE)

Function Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Gets the ServiceManager Templates from an AutomateNOW! instance

    .DESCRIPTION
    Gets the ServiceManager Templates from an AutomateNOW! instance

    .PARAMETER Id
    Mandatory string containing the simple id of the ServiceManager Template to fetch or you can pipeline a series of simple id strings. You may not enter an array here.

    .PARAMETER Type
    Mandatory string containing the type of ServiceManager Template. Valid choices are SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER, PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR. Note this is a custom class!

    .PARAMETER sortBy
    Optional string parameter to sort the results by. Valid choices are: id {To be continued...}

    .PARAMETER Descending
    Optional switch parameter to sort in descending order

    .PARAMETER startRow
    Optional integer to indicate the row to start from. This is intended for when you need to paginate the results. Default is 0.

    .PARAMETER endRow
    Optional integer to indicate the row to stop on. This is intended for when you need to paginate the results. Default is 100.

    .PARAMETER Folder
    Optional string to filter by a particular Folder

    .PARAMETER Tags
    Optional string array of Tags to filter by. Note that the 'containsAny' operator will be used.

    .INPUTS
    Accepts a string representing the simple id of the ServiceManager Template from the pipeline or individually (but not an array).

    .OUTPUTS
    An array of one or more [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] class objects

    .EXAMPLE
    Gets the first page of Service Manager Templates
    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    .EXAMPLE
    Gets a specific Server Manager Template by Id
    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManager1'

    .EXAMPLE
    Gets the first page of Service Level Agreement Template objects
    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Type SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER

    .EXAMPLE
    Gets the first page of Processing Deadline Monitor Template objects
    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Type PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR

    .EXAMPLE
    Uses the pipeline to send two names to fetch the Service Manager Templates by Id.
    @( 'ServiceManager1', 'ServiceManager2' ) | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    .EXAMPLE
    Gets all ServiceManager Templates that are tagged with 'Tag1'
    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Tags 'Tag1'

    .NOTES
    You must use Connect-AutomateNOW to establish the token by way of global variable.

    #>
    [OutputType([ANOWServiceManagerTemplate[]])]
    [CmdletBinding()]
    Param(
        [ValidateScript({ $_ -match '^[0-9a-zA-Z_.-]{1,}$' })]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $False, ValueFromPipeline = $true)]
        [string]$Id,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $False)]
        [ANOWProcessingTemplateCustom_ServiceManagers]$Type,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $False)]
        [string]$sortBy = 'id',
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $False)]
        [switch]$Descending,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $False)]
        [int32]$startRow = 0,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $False)]
        [int32]$endRow = 100,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $False)]
        [string]$Folder,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $False)]
        [string[]]$Tags
    )
    Begin {
        If ((Confirm-AutomateNOWSession -Quiet) -ne $true) {
            Write-Warning -Message "There is not a valid token confirmed."
            Break
        }
        If ($Tags.Count -gt 0) {
            ForEach ($tag_id in $Tags) {
                $Error.Clear()
                Try {
                    [ANOWTag]$tag_object = Get-AutomateNOWTag -Id $tag_id
                }
                Catch {
                    [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
                    Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWTag had an error while retrieving the tag [$tag_id] running under Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate due to [$Message]"
                    Break
                }
                If ($tag_object.simpleId.length -eq 0) {
                    Throw "Get-AutomateNOWTag failed to confirm that the tag [$tag_id] actually exists under Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate. Please check the tag name and try again."
                }
            }
        }
        If ($endRow -le $startRow) {
            Write-Warning -Message "The endRow must be greater than the startRow. Please try again."
            Break
        }
        [hashtable]$parameters = @{}
        $parameters.Add('Method', 'GET')
        If ($anow_session.NotSecure -eq $true) {
            $parameters.Add('NotSecure', $true)
        }
    }
    Process {
        [System.Collections.Specialized.OrderedDictionary]$BodyMetaData = [System.Collections.Specialized.OrderedDictionary]@{}
        $BodyMetaData.'_constructor' = 'AdvancedCriteria'
        $BodyMetaData.'operator' = 'and'
        $BodyMetaData.'_operationType' = 'fetch'
        $BodyMetaData.'_startRow' = $startRow
        $BodyMetaData.'_endRow' = $endRow
        $BodyMetaData.'_componentId' = 'ProcessingTemplateList'
        $BodyMetaData.'_dataSource' = 'ProcessingTemplateDataSource'
        $BodyMetaData.'isc_metaDataPrefix' = '_'
        $BodyMetaData.'isc_dataFormat' = 'json'
        If ($Descending -eq $true) {
            $BodyMetaData.'_sortBy' = '-' + $sortBy
        }
        Else {
            $BodyMetaData.'_sortBy' = $sortBy
        }
        If ($_.Length -gt 0 -or $Id.Length -gt 0) {
            If ($_.Length -gt 0 ) {
                $BodyMetaData.'id' = $_
            }
            Else {
                $BodyMetaData.'id' = $Id
            }
            [string]$textMatchStyle = 'exactCase'
        }
        Else {
            [string]$textMatchStyle = 'substring'
            If ( $Type.length -eq 0) {
                $BodyMetaData.'criteria1' = '{"_constructor":"AdvancedCriteria","operator":"or","criteria":[{"fieldName":"monitorType","operator":"inSet","value":["PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR"]},{"fieldName":"serviceManagerType","operator":"inSet","value":["SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER"]}]}'
            }
            Else {
                If ($Type -eq 'SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER') {
                    $BodyMetaData.'criteria1' = ('{"fieldName":"serviceManagerType","operator":"equals","value":["SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER"]}')
                }
                ElseIf ($Type -eq 'PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR') {
                    $BodyMetaData.'criteria1' = ('{"fieldName":"monitorType","operator":"equals","value":["PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR"]}')
                }
                Else {
                    Write-Warning -Message "Unable to determine the type of Service Manager Template being requested."
                    Break
                }
            }
            If ($Folder.Length -gt 0) {
                $BodyMetaData.'criteria2' = ('{"fieldName":"folder","operator":"equals","value":"' + $Folder + '"}')
            }
            If ($Tags.Count -gt 0) {
                If ($Tags.Count -gt 1) {
                    $Error.Clear()
                    Try {
                        [string]$TagString = $Tags | ConvertTo-JSON -Compress -Depth 100
                    }
                    Catch {
                        [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
                        Write-Warning -Message "ConvertTo-Json failed to convert the provided tag names under Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate due to [$Message]."
                        Break
                    }
                }
                Else {
                    [string]$TagString = $Tags
                }
                $BodyMetaData.'criteria3' = ('{"fieldName":"tags","operator":"containsAny","value":' + $TagString + '}')
            }
        }
        $BodyMetaData.'_textMatchStyle' = $textMatchStyle
        [string]$Body = ConvertTo-QueryString -InputObject $BodyMetaData
        [string]$command = ('/processingTemplate/read?' + $Body)
        If ($null -eq $parameters["Command"]) {
            $parameters.Add('Command', $command)
        }
        Else {
            $parameters.Command = $command
        }
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            [PSCustomObject]$results = Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI @parameters
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            Write-Warning -Message "Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI failed to execute [$command] due to [$Message]."
            Break
        }
        [int32]$response_code = $results.response.status
        If ($response_code -ne 0) {
            [string]$full_response_display = $results.response | ConvertTo-Json -Compress -Depth 100
            Write-Warning -Message "The response code was not 0 but was [$response_code]. Body: $full_response_display"
            Break
        }
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate[]]$ServiceManagerTemplates = $results.response.data
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            Write-Warning -Message "Failed to parse the response into a series of [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects due to [$Message]."
            Break
        }
        If ($ServiceManagerTemplates.Count -gt 0) {
            ForEach ($ServiceManagerTemplate in $ServiceManagerTemplates) {
                If ($ServiceManagerTemplate.processingType -ne 'SERVICE') {
                    [string]$processingType = $ServiceManagerTemplate.processingType
                    If ($processingType -in @('TASK')) {
                        Write-Warning -Message "$Id is actually a Task Template. Please use Get-AutomateNOWTaskTemplate to retrieve this item."
                    }
                    ElseIf ($processingType -eq 'WORKFLOW') {
                        Write-Warning -Message "$Id is actually a Workflow Template. Please use Get-AutomateNOWWorkflowTemplate to retrieve this item."
                    }
                    ElseIf ($processingType -eq 'TRIGGER') {
                        Write-Warning -Message "$Id is actually a Schedule Template. Please use Get-AutomateNOWScheduleTemplate to retrieve this item."
                    }
                    Else {
                        Write-Warning -Message "Could not identify what type of template object [$processingType] is..."
                    }
                    Break
                }
            }
            Return $ServiceManagerTemplates
        }
    }
    End {

    }
}

Function Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Changes the settings of a Service Manager Template on an AutomateNOW! instance

    .DESCRIPTION
    Changes selected Service Manager Template fields while preserving the complete
    processingCommand and unselected serviceMode settings independently per input.
    Caller objects are unchanged. A clean acknowledgment and one matching strict
    result are required, including with Quiet. Uncertain diagnostics stop later
    inputs without retry; a failed result does not undo an acknowledged write.

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerTemplate
    An [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object representing the Service Manager Template to be changed.

    .PARAMETER ProcessingTemplate
    An [ANOWProcessingTemplate] object representing the Processing Template to be monitored. Workflow Templates, Task Templates, Schedule Templates and Service Manager Templates may be submitted here (applies to Processing Deadline Monitors only)

    .PARAMETER UnsetProcessingTemplate
    Optional switch that will remove the Processing Template from the Service Manager Template object (applies to Processing Deadline Monitors only)

    .PARAMETER Description
    Optional description of the Service Manager Template (may not exceed 255 characters).

    .PARAMETER UnsetDescription
    Optional switch that will remove the Description from the Service Manager Template object.

    .PARAMETER Folder
    A string representing the name of the Folder to move the Service Manager Template into.

    .PARAMETER UnsetFolder
    A switch parameter that will move the Service Manager Template out of its current folder.

    .PARAMETER Tags
    Optional string array of CASE-SENSITIVE Tag Id's to assign to this Service Manager Template. You must specify all of the Tags.

    .PARAMETER UnsetTags
    A switch parameter that will remove the Tags from the Service Manager Template

    .PARAMETER CodeRepository
    Optional Code Repository to place the Service Manager Template into. Use Get-AutomateNOWCodeRepository to fetch this object.

    .PARAMETER UnsetCodeRepository
    A switch parameter that will remove the Service Manager Template from its Code Repository.

    .PARAMETER RunMode
    Selects ONCE, COUNTER, FOR or UNTIL. Omission preserves each input's current
    mode and all unselected settings. Explicit modes retain their required run
    arguments. Changing mode removes inactive known mode fields and retains opaque
    command/mode siblings; selecting the same mode retains unbound settings.

    .PARAMETER RunInterval
    Milliseconds between checks for COUNTER, FOR and UNTIL. Required with an
    explicit selection of those modes; otherwise only a supplied value is edited.
    Omitted values and the existing -1 sentinel preserve the stored interval.
    For example, 300000 means five minutes.

    .PARAMETER RunTimes
    An int64 specifying how many total times the Service Level Agreement will check. Applies only to 'COUNTER' run mode.

    .PARAMETER RunFor
    An int64 span of time in milliseconds Specifies how long the Service Level Agreement remains active. Applies only to 'FOR' run mode. For example, set this to 86400000 for the Service Level Agreement to run for 1 day.

    .PARAMETER RunTimeOfDay
    An int64 specifying the time of day until which the Service Level Agreement remains active. Applies only to 'UNTIL' run mode. For example, set this to 86399999 for 23:59:59.999 which is the maximum possible value.

    .PARAMETER RunTimeZone
    An [ANOWTimeZone] object that specifies the time zone [that] the Service Level Agreement follows. Applies only to 'UNTIL' run mode. Use Get-AutomateNOWTimeZone to fetch this object.

    .PARAMETER RunOffSet
    Optional UNTIL dayOffset. An explicit zero sets zero; omission preserves the
    existing offset on unchanged mode. A mode transition with no offset omits it.

    .PARAMETER Title
    A string representing the "alias" of the Service Manager Template (this property needs a better explanation)

    .PARAMETER UnsetTitle
    A switch parameter that will remove the Title from the Service Manager Template

    .PARAMETER ResultMapping
    An [ResultMapping] object representing the Result Mapping object to set on the Service Manager Template.

    .PARAMETER UnsetResultMapping
    A switch parameter that will remove the Result Mapping assignment from the Service Manager Template.

    .PARAMETER Calendar
    An [ANOWCalendar] object representing the Calendar object to set on the Service Manager Template. Use Get-AutomateNOWCalendar to fetch one of these.

    .PARAMETER UnsetCalendar
    A switch parameter that will remove the Calendar assignment from the Service Manager Template.

    .PARAMETER DelayedStartTime
    Optional string that allows processing items to start on a specific date or time or delay the execution for a period ranging from days to seconds. Example 1: 2029-12-31, Example 2: 2029-12-31 23:59:59, Example 3: 23:59:59

    .PARAMETER UnsetDelayedStartTime
    A switch parameter that will remove the Delayed Start Time from the Service Manager Template.

    .PARAMETER TimeZone
    Optional [ANOWTimeZone] object that modifies (it is unknown exactly what this property modifies since it is not defined in the documentation yet). Use Get-AutomateNOWTimeZone to fetch this object.

    .PARAMETER UnsetTimeZone
    A switch parameter that will remove the Time Zone from the Service Manager Template.

    .PARAMETER Approval
    A [ANOWApproval] object representing the Approval object to set on the Service Manager Template.

    .PARAMETER UnsetApproval
    A switch parameter that will remove the Approval assignment from the Service Manager Template.

    .PARAMETER Priority
    An integer representing the items priority which determines the order when queuing for resources (Stock and Locks) and [for] being executed by Server Nodes. Default Priority is 0. Minimal Priority is 0.

    .PARAMETER Weight
    An integer representing a logical measure of resources required to process the item by the Server Node. Each Server Node has [a] maximum weight capacity[.] Weight determines [the] number of parallel processes that can run simultaneously. Default processing Weight is 1. Minimal Weight is 0.

    .PARAMETER MaxSimultaneousExecutions
    An optional integer that limits how many executions of this Service Manager Template may run at the same time. The UI allows this value to be cleared back to blank, which is treated as null.

    .PARAMETER UnsetMaxSimultaneousExecutions
    A switch parameter that will remove the Max Simultaneous Executions value from the Service Manager Template and send it as blank or null.

    .PARAMETER Hold
    A boolean to put the Service Manager Template on Hold status. You must specify $true or $false here. When $true, it's the same as the Suspend-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate function. When $false, Resume-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate function.

    .PARAMETER Skip
    A boolean to put the Service Manager Template on Skip status. You must specify $true or $false here. When $true, it's the same as the Skip-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate function. When $false, Skip-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate with -UnSkip parameter.

    .PARAMETER IgnoreProcessingRegistry
    A boolean setting that enables 'Ignore Processing Registry' on the Task. You must specify $true or $false here.

    .PARAMETER VerboseMode
    A boolean setting that enables Verbose Mode on the Service Managers from this Service Manager Template. You must specify $true or $false here.

    .PARAMETER AutoArchive
    A boolean that causes the Service Managers from this Service Manager Template to be archived immediately after execution. You must specify $true or $false here.

    .PARAMETER KeepResources
    A boolean that indicates if the Service Managers from this Service Manager Template should keep its resources (Stocks and Locks) and reuse them on the restart so that they are not consumed by other tasks or workflows. You must specify $true or $false here.

    .PARAMETER UseScripts
    A boolean that enables support for Pre and Post scripts within this Service Manager Template

    .PARAMETER EagerScriptExecution
    A boolean that indicates if the scripts from the Service Managers from this Service Manager Template should use "Eager" load strategy. In order to use this parameter, you must include -UseScripts $true.

    .PARAMETER Owner
    An optional decorational string to indicate who the "owner" of this object is.

    .PARAMETER statisticalDuration
    An int64 number in milliseconds of the expected duration of the Service Manager Template. The minimum/maximum is 1000/31536000000 (1 second/1 year). The default is 60000 (1 minute).

    .PARAMETER Force
    Force the change without confirmation. This is equivalent to -Confirm:$false

    .PARAMETER Quiet
    Switch parameter that silences the output of the updated object.

    .INPUTS
    ONLY [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects are accepted (including from the pipeline)

    .OUTPUTS
    The updated [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object will be returned

    .EXAMPLE
    Forcefully and quietly sets the description, folder, tags, code repository, title, result mapping, calendar, approval, time zone, delayed start time, priority, weight, enables Hold, enables Skip, enables IgnoreProcessingRegistry, enables VerboseMode, enables AutoArchive, enables KeepResources, enables UseScripts, enables EagerScriptExecution, the Owner and the statisticalDuration is set to 30 seconds (multi-line format)

    $service_manager_template = Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManagerTemplate1'
    $code_repo = Get-AutomateNOWCodeRepository -Id 'CodeRepository1'
    $result_mapping = Get-AutomateNOWResultMapping -Id 'ResultMapping1'
    $calendar = Get-AutomateNOWCalendar -Id 'Calendar1'
    $approval = Get-AutomateNOWApproval -Id 'Approval1'
    $time_zone = Get-AutomateNOWTimeZone -Id 'UTC'

    Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate $service_manager_template -Description 'Description1' -Folder 'Folder1' -Tags 'Tag1', 'Tag2' -CodeRepository $code_repo -Title 'Title1' -ResultMapping $result_mapping -Calendar $calendar -Approval $approval -TimeZone $time_zone -DelayedStartTime 2030-12-31 -Priority 5 -Weight 5 -Hold $true -Skip $true -IgnoreProcessingRegistry $true -VerboseMode $true -AutoArchive $true -KeepResources $true -UseScripts $true -EagerScriptExecution $true -Owner 'Owner1' -statisticalDuration 30000 -Quiet -Force

    .EXAMPLE
    Sets the description, folder, tags, code repository, title, result mapping, calendar, approval, time zone, delayed start time, priority, weight, enables Hold, enables Skip, enables IgnoreProcessingRegistry, enables VerboseMode, enables AutoArchive, enables KeepResources, enables UseScripts, enables EagerScriptExecution, the Owner and the statisticalDuration is set to 30 seconds (one-liner format)

    Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate (Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManagerTemplate1') -Description 'Description1' -Folder 'Folder1' -Tags 'Tag1', 'Tag2' -CodeRepository (Get-AutomateNOWCodeRepository -Id 'CodeRepository1') -Title 'Title1' -ResultMapping (Get-AutomateNOWResultMapping -Id 'ResultMapping1') -Calendar (Get-AutomateNOWCalendar -Id 'Calendar1') -DelayedStartTime 2030-12-31 -TimeZone (Get-AutomateNOWTimeZone -Id 'UTC') -Approval (Get-AutomateNOWApproval -Id 'Approval1') -Priority 5 -Weight 5 -Hold $true -Skip $true -IgnoreProcessingRegistry $true -VerboseMode $true -AutoArchive $true -KeepResources $true -UseScripts $true -EagerScriptExecution $true -Owner 'Owner1' -statisticalDuration 30000 -Quiet -Force

    .EXAMPLE
    Unsets the description, folder, tags, code repository, title, result mapping, calendar, approval, time zone, delayed start time, disables Hold, disables Skip, disables IgnoreProcessingRegistry, disables VerboseMode, disables AutoArchive, disables KeepResources, disables UseScripts, disables EagerScriptExecution (one-liner format)

    Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate (Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManagerTemplate1') -UnsetDescription -UnsetFolder -UnsetTags -UnsetCodeRepository -UnsetTitle -UnsetResultMapping -UnsetCalendar -UnsetApproval -UnsetTimeZone -UnsetDelayedStartTime -Hold $false -Skip $false -IgnoreProcessingRegistry $false -VerboseMode $false -AutoArchive $false -KeepResources $false -UseScripts $false -EagerScriptExecution $false -Quiet -Force

    .EXAMPLE
    Forcefully and quietly sets the Run Mode of a Service Manager Template named 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' to 'ONCE'

    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' | Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -RunMode 'ONCE' -Force -Quiet

    .EXAMPLE
    Quietly sets the Run Mode of a Service Manager Template named 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' to 'COUNTER' that will run every 60 minutes for a total of 12 times.

    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' | Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -RunMode 'COUNTER' -RunInterval 3600000 -RunTimes 12 -Quiet

    .EXAMPLE
    Sets the Run Mode of a Service Manager Template named 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' to 'FOR' that will run once a day for a year.

    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' | Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -RunMode 'FOR' -RunInterval 86400000 -RunFor 31536000000

    .EXAMPLE
    Sets the Run Mode of a Service Manager Template named 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' to 'UNTIL' that will run every 30 minutes until 12:00pm in the UTC timezone

    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' | Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -RunMode 'UNTIL' -RunInterval 1800000 -RunTimeZone (Get-AutomateNOWTimeZone -Id 'UTC') -RunTimeOfDay 43200000

    .EXAMPLE
    Forcefully sets the 'processing template to monitor' on a Processing Deadline Monitor named 'ProcessingDeadlineMonitor1' to a Task Template named 'TaskTemplate1' (multi-line)

    $processing_deadline_monitor = Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ProcessingDeadlineMonitor1'
    $processing_deadline_monitor | Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ProcessingTemplate (Get-AutomateNOWTaskTemplate -Id 'TaskTemplate1') -Force

    .EXAMPLE
    Forcefully unsets the 'processing template to monitor' on a Processing Deadline Monitor named 'ProcessingDeadlineMonitor1' (multi-line)

    $processing_deadline_monitor = Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ProcessingDeadlineMonitor1'
    $processing_deadline_monitor | Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -UnsetProcessingTemplate -Force

    .NOTES

    You must use Connect-AutomateNOW to establish the token by way of global variable.

    About Run Modes:

    Once
    ----
    Checks if all the Processing Deadline Monitor items inside the SLA are completed one time upon execution.

    Given Number of Times
    ---------------------
    Checks if all the Processing Deadline Monitor items are completed in a specified number of times at a set interval.
        - Run Times - Specifies how many times the Service Level Agreement checks.
        - Run Interval - Specifies the time interval between checks.

    Periodically for period of times
    --------------------------------
    Checks if all the Processing Deadline Monitor items are completed within a specific duration at a set interval.
        - Run For - Specifies how long the Service Level Agreement remains active.
        - Run Interval - Specifies the time interval between checks.

    Periodically until given time of day
    ------------------------------------
    Checks if all the Processing Deadline Monitor items are completed until a specified time.
        - Run Until Time - Specifies the time of day until which the Service Level Agreement remains active.
        - Add Day Offset - Shifts the SLA end time's date by the specified number of days. Defaults to 0 which means the SLA ends on the same day it starts.
        - Time Zone - Specifies the time zone [that] the Service Level Agreement follows.
        - Run Interval - Specifies the time interval between checks.
    #>
    [OutputType([ANOWServiceManagerTemplate])]
    [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess, ConfirmImpact = 'High')]
    Param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ValueFromPipeline = $True)]
        [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWProcessingTemplate]$ProcessingTemplate,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetProcessingTemplate,
        [ValidateScript({ $_.Length -le 255 })]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$Description,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetDescription,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$Folder,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetFolder,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string[]]$Tags,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetTags,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWCodeRepository]$CodeRepository,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetCodeRepository,
        [ValidateSet('ONCE', 'COUNTER', 'FOR', 'UNTIL')]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$RunMode,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int64]$RunInterval = -1,        # applies to 'COUNTER', 'FOR' and 'UNTIL' mode
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int64]$RunTimes = -1,           # applies to 'COUNTER' mode only
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int64]$RunFor = -1,             # applies to 'FOR' mode only
        [ValidateRange(0, 86399999)]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int64]$RunTimeOfDay = -1,       # applies to 'UNTIL' mode only
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWTimeZone]$RunTimeZone,      # applies to 'UNTIL' mode only
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int32]$RunOffSet,               # applies to 'UNTIL' mode only
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$Title,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetTitle,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWResultMapping]$ResultMapping,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetResultMapping,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWCalendar]$Calendar,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetCalendar,
        [ValidateScript({ $_ -match '([0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}){0,}( {0,}[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}){0,}' })]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$DelayedStartTime,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetDelayedStartTime,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWTimeZone]$TimeZone,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetTimeZone,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWApproval]$Approval,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetApproval,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int32]$Priority = -1,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int32]$Weight = -1,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[int32]]$MaxSimultaneousExecutions = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetMaxSimultaneousExecutions,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[boolean]]$Hold = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[boolean]]$Skip = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[boolean]]$IgnoreProcessingRegistry = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[boolean]]$VerboseMode = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[boolean]]$AutoArchive = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[boolean]]$KeepResources = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[boolean]]$UseScripts = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [Nullable[boolean]]$EagerScriptExecution = $null,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$Owner,
        [ValidateRange(1000, 31536000000)]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int64]$statisticalDuration,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Force,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Quiet
    )
    Begin {
        $preservationStopped=$false
        $options=@{}
        foreach ($key in $PSBoundParameters.Keys) { $options[$key]=$PSBoundParameters[$key] }
        if ($Force -and $PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Confirm') -and $PSBoundParameters['Confirm']) { $Force=$false }
        if (-not (Confirm-ANOWPreservationSession)) {
            $preservationStopped=$true
            Write-Warning -Message 'Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate stopped at [session]; no update was submitted.'
        } elseif (-not (Test-ANOWPreservationValidation -Kind 'ServiceManagerTemplate' -Options $options)) {
            $preservationStopped=$true
            Write-Warning -Message 'Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate stopped at [options]; no update was submitted.'
        }
    }
    Process {
        if (-not $preservationStopped) {
            $dispatched=$false; $acknowledged=$false; $failed=$false; $stage='input validation'
            do {
                if (-not (Test-ANOWPreservationValidation -Kind 'ServiceManagerTemplate' -Target $ServiceManagerTemplate -Options $options)) { $failed=$true; break }
                If (($Force -eq $true -and -not $WhatIfPreference) -or ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($ServiceManagerTemplate.id)) -eq $true) {
                    $stage='prerequisite/preparation'
                    $prepared=Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command New-ANOWPreservationRequest) -OperationParameters @{Kind='ServiceManagerTemplate';Target=$ServiceManagerTemplate;Options=$options}
                    if (-not $prepared.Succeeded -or @($prepared.Data).Count -ne 1) { $failed=$true; break }
                    $request=$prepared.Data[0]
                    foreach ($advisory in $request.Advisories) { Write-Warning -Message $advisory }
                    $parameters=@{Command=$request.Command;Body=$request.Body;Method='POST';ContentType='application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=UTF-8'}
                    if ($anow_session.NotSecure -eq $true) { $parameters['NotSecure']=$true }
                    $stage='API';$dispatched=$true
                    $result=Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI) -OperationParameters $parameters
                    if (-not $result.Succeeded) { $failed=$true; break }
                    $stage='acknowledgment'
                    if (-not (Test-ANOWPreservationAcknowledgment -Envelopes $result.Data)) { $failed=$true; break }
                    $acknowledged=$true
                    $stage='strict result'
                    $conversion=Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command ConvertFrom-ANOWPreservationResponse) -OperationParameters @{Kind='ServiceManagerTemplate';Envelopes=$result.Data;Target=$ServiceManagerTemplate;Options=$options}
                    if (-not $conversion.Succeeded -or @($conversion.Data).Count -ne 1) { $failed=$true; break }
                    $updated=$conversion.Data[0]
                    Write-Verbose -Message "ServiceManagerTemplate object [$($ServiceManagerTemplate.id)] was successfully updated"

                    if (-not $Quiet) { $updated }
                }
            } while ($false)
            if ($failed) {
                $preservationStopped=$true
                $effect=if ($acknowledged) { 'The write was acknowledged; its result/readback was not verified.' } elseif ($dispatched) { 'The write may have occurred; its outcome was not verified.' } else { 'No update was submitted.' }
                Write-Warning -Message "Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate stopped at [$stage]. $effect No retry or rollback was attempted."
            }
        }
    }
}

Function Export-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Exports the ServiceManager Templates from an instance of AutomateNOW!

    .DESCRIPTION
    Exports the ServiceManager Templates from an instance of AutomateNOW! to a local .csv file

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerTemplate
    Mandatory [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object (Use Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate to retrieve them)

    .INPUTS
    ONLY [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects from the pipeline are accepted

    .OUTPUTS
    The [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects are exported to the local disk in CSV format

    .EXAMPLE
    Exports the first page of Service Manager Templates (one-liner)

    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate | Export-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    .EXAMPLE
    Exports 2 Service Manager Templates by name/id (one-liner)

    'ServiceManagerTemplate1', 'ServiceManagerTemplate2' | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate | Export-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    .NOTES
    You must present [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects to the pipeline to use this function.

    #>

    [CmdletBinding(DefaultParameterSetName = 'Pipeline')]
    Param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ValueFromPipeline = $true, ParameterSetName = 'Pipeline')]
        [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate
    )
    Begin {
        [string]$current_time = Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMddHHmmssfff'
        [string]$ExportFileName = 'Export-AutomateNOW-ServiceManagerTemplates-' + $current_time + '.csv'
        [string]$ExportFilePath = ((Get-Location | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Path) + '\' + $ExportFileName)
        [hashtable]$parameters = @{}
        $parameters.Add('Path', $ExportFilePath)
        $parameters.Add('Append', $true)
        If ($PSVersionTable.PSVersion.Major -eq 5) {
            $parameters.Add('NoTypeInformation', $true)
        }
    }
    Process {
        If ($_.id.Length -gt 0) {
            [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate = $_
        }
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            $ServiceManagerTemplate | Export-CSV @parameters
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            Write-Warning -Message "Export-CSV failed to export the [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object on the pipeline due to [$Message]"
            Break
        }
    }
    End {
        $Error.Clear()
        If ((Test-Path -Path $ExportFilePath) -eq $true) {
            [System.IO.FileInfo]$fileinfo = Get-Item -Path "$ExportFilePath"
            [int32]$filelength = $fileinfo.Length
            [string]$filelength_display = "{0:N0}" -f $filelength
            Write-Information -MessageData "Created file $ExportFileName ($filelength_display bytes)"
        }
    }
}

Function New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Creates a Service Manager Template within an AutomateNOW! instance

    .DESCRIPTION
    Creates a Service Manager Template within an AutomateNOW! instance and returns back the newly created [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object

    .PARAMETER Id
    Mandatory "name" of the ServiceManager Template. For example: 'ServiceManagerTemplate1'. This value may not contain the domain in brackets. This is the unique key of this object.

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerType
    Required type of the Service Manager Template. Valid choices are: SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER or PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR

    .PARAMETER Description
    Optional description of the Service Manager Template (may not exceed 255 characters).

    .PARAMETER Tags
    Optional string array of CASE-SENSITIVE Tag Id's to include with this object.

    .PARAMETER Folder
    Optional string representing the Folder to place this object into.

    .PARAMETER DesignTemplate
    An optional [ANOWDesignTemplate] object to apply to the newly created Service Manager Template. Use Get-AutomateNOWDesignTemplate to obtain these objects.

    .PARAMETER Workspace
    Optional string representing the Workspace to place this object into.

    .PARAMETER CodeRepository
    Optional name of the code repository to place the ServiceManager into.

    .PARAMETER Quiet
    Optional switch to suppress the return of the newly created object

    .INPUTS
    None. You cannot pipe objects to New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate.

    .OUTPUTS
    An [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object representing the newly created ServiceManager Template. Use the -Quiet parameter to suppress this.

    .EXAMPLE
    Quietly creates a new Service Manager Template (of type SLA Service Manager) named 'ServiceLevelAgreement1' with a description, tags, folder, workspace and code repository (one-liner)

    New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceLevelAgreement1' -ServiceManagerType SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER -Description 'Description1' -Tags 'Tag1', 'Tag2' -Folder 'Folder1' -Workspace 'Workspace1' -CodeRepository (Get-AutomateNOWCodeRepository -Id 'CodeRepository1') -Quiet

    .EXAMPLE
    Quietly creates a new Service Manager Template (of type Processing Deadline Monitor) named 'ProcessingDeadlineMonitor1' with a description, tags, folder, workspace and code repository (one-liner)

    New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ProcessingDeadlineMonitor1' -ServiceManagerType PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR -Description 'Description1' -Tags 'Tag1', 'Tag2' -Folder 'Folder1' -Workspace 'Workspace1' -CodeRepository (Get-AutomateNOWCodeRepository -Id 'CodeRepository1') -Quiet

    .NOTES
    You must use Connect-AutomateNOW to establish the token by way of global variable.

    The name (id) of the ServiceManager Template must be unique (per domain). It may consist only of letters, numbers, underscore, dot or hyphen.

    To set the Processing Template to monitor for a processing deadline monitor, use Set-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    #>
    [OutputType([ANOWServiceManagerTemplate])]
    [CmdletBinding()]
    Param(
        [ValidateScript({ $_ -match '^[0-9a-zA-Z_.-]{1,}$' })]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
        [string]$Id,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
        [ANOWProcessingTemplateCustom_ServiceManagers]$ServiceManagerType,
        [ValidateScript({ $_.Length -le 255 })]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false, HelpMessage = "Enter a descriptive string up to 255 characters (UTF8 compatible)")]
        [string]$Description,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string[]]$Tags,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$Folder,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWDesignTemplate]$DesignTemplate,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$Workspace,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWCodeRepository]$CodeRepository,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Quiet
    )
    If ((Confirm-AutomateNOWSession -Quiet) -ne $true) {
        Write-Warning -Message "There is not a valid token confirmed."
        Break
    }
    ## Begin warning ##
    ## Do not tamper with this below code which makes sure that the object exists before attempting to change it.
    $Error.Clear()
    Try {
        [boolean]$ServiceManagerTemplate_exists = ($null -ne (Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id $Id))
    }
    Catch {
        [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
        Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate failed to check if the ServiceManager Template [$Id] already existed due to [$Message]."
        Break
    }
    If ($ServiceManagerTemplate_exists -eq $true) {
        [string]$current_domain = $anow_session.header.domain
        Write-Warning -Message "There is already a ServiceManager Template named [$Id] in [$current_domain]."
        Break
    }
    ## End warning ##
    [System.Collections.Specialized.OrderedDictionary]$BodyMetaData = [System.Collections.Specialized.OrderedDictionary]@{}
    $BodyMetaData.Add('id', $Id)
    $BodyMetaData.Add('processingType', 'SERVICE')
    $BodyMetaData.Add('serverNodeType', 'INTERNAL')
    If ($ServiceManagerType -eq 'SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER') {
        $BodyMetaData.Add('serviceManagerType', 'SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER')
        $BodyMetaData.Add('serviceType', 'SERVICE_MANAGER')
        [string]$old_values = '{"processingType":"SERVICE","serviceType":"SERVICE_MANAGER","serviceManagerType":"SLA_SERVICE_MANAGER","workspace":null,"serverNodeType":"INTERNAL"}'
    }
    ElseIf ($ServiceManagerType -eq 'PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR') {
        $BodyMetaData.Add('monitorType', 'PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR')
        $BodyMetaData.Add('serviceType', 'MONITOR')
        [string]$old_values = '{"processingType":"SERVICE","serviceType":"MONITOR","monitorType":"PROCESSING_DEADLINE_MONITOR","workspace":null,"serverNodeType":"INTERNAL"}'
    }
    Else {
        Write-Warning -Message "It was not possible to determine the type of Service Manager Template that was to be created."
        Break
    }
    If ($Description.Length -gt 0) {
        $BodyMetaData.Add('description', $Description)
    }
    If ($Tags.Count -gt 0) {
        [int32]$current_tag = 1
        ForEach ($tag_id in $Tags) {
            $Error.Clear()
            Try {
                [ANOWTag]$tag_object = Get-AutomateNOWTag -Id $tag_id
            }
            Catch {
                [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
                Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWTag had an error while retrieving the tag [$tag_id] under New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate due to [$Message]"
                Break
            }
            If ($tag_object.simpleId.length -eq 0) {
                Throw "New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate has detected that the tag [$tag_id] does not appear to exist."
            }
            ElseIf (($tag_object.simpleId -eq $tag_id) -and ($tag_object.simpleId -cne $tag_id)) {
                [string]$tag_object_simpleId = $tag_object.simpleId
                Throw "Wait! Tags are case-sensitive. [$tag_object_simpleId] is not the same case as [$tag_id]. Please check more carefully..."
            }
            [string]$tag_name_sequence = ('tags' + $current_tag)
            $BodyMetaData.Add($tag_name_sequence, $tag_id)
            $current_tag++
        }
    }
    If ($Folder.Length -gt 0) {
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            [ANOWFolder]$folder_object = Get-AutomateNOWFolder -Id $Folder
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWFolder failed to confirm that the folder [$Folder] actually existed while running under New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate due to [$Message]"
            Break
        }
        If ($folder_object.simpleId.Length -eq 0) {
            Throw "Get-AutomateNOWFolder failed to locate the Folder [$Folder] running under New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate."
        }
        [string]$folder_display = $folder_object | ConvertTo-JSON -Compress -Depth 100
        Write-Verbose -Message "Adding folder $folder_display to [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] [$Id]"
        $BodyMetaData.Add('folder', $Folder)
    }
    If ($DesignTemplate.id.Length -gt 0) {
        [string]$DesignTemplateId = $DesignTemplate.id
        Write-Verbose -Message "Adding Design Template $DesignTemplateId to [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] [$Id]"
        $BodyMetaData.Add('designTemplate', $DesignTemplateId)
    }
    If ($Workspace.Length -gt 0) {
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            [ANOWWorkspace]$workspace_object = Get-AutomateNOWWorkspace -Id $Workspace
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            [string]$Workspace_id = $Workspace.Id
            Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWWorkspace failed to confirm that the workspace [$Workspace_id] actually existed while running under New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate due to [$Message]"
            Break
        }
        If ($workspace_object.simpleId.Length -eq 0) {
            Throw "Get-AutomateNOWWorkspace failed to locate the Workspace [$Workspace] running under New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate."
        }
        [string]$workspace_display = $workspace_object | ConvertTo-JSON -Compress -Depth 100
        Write-Verbose -Message "Adding workspace $workspace_display to [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] [$Id]"
        $BodyMetaData.Add('workspace', $Workspace)
    }
    If ($CodeRepository.id.Length -gt 0) {
        [string]$CodeRepository_Id = $CodeRepository.id
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            [ANOWCodeRepository]$code_repository_object = Get-AutomateNOWCodeRepository -Id $CodeRepository_Id
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWCodeRepository failed to confirm that the code repository [$CodeRepository_Id] existed under New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate due to [$Message]"
            Break
        }
        If ($code_repository_object.simpleId.Length -eq 0) {
            Throw "Get-AutomateNOWCodeRepository failed to locate the Code Repository [$CodeRepository_Id] under New-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate."
        }
        Write-Verbose -Message "Adding Service Manager Template [$Id] to Code Repository $CodeRepository_Id"
        $BodyMetaData.'codeRepository' = $CodeRepository_Id
    }
    $BodyMetaData.'_textMatchStyle' = 'exact'
    $BodyMetaData.'_operationType' = 'add'
    $BodyMetaData.'_oldValues' = $old_values
    $BodyMetaData.'_componentId' = 'ProcessingTemplateCreateWindow_form'
    $BodyMetaData.'_dataSource' = 'ProcessingTemplateDataSource'
    $BodyMetaData.'isc_metaDataPrefix' = '_'
    $BodyMetaData.'isc_dataFormat' = 'json'
    [string]$Body = ConvertTo-QueryString -InputObject $BodyMetaData
    [string]$command = '/processingTemplate/create'
    [hashtable]$parameters = @{}
    $parameters.Add('ContentType', 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=UTF-8')
    $parameters.Add('Command', $command)
    $parameters.Add('Method', 'POST')
    $parameters.Add('Body', $Body)
    If ($anow_session.NotSecure -eq $true) {
        $parameters.Add('NotSecure', $true)
    }
    [string]$parameters_display = $parameters | ConvertTo-JSON -Compress -Depth 100
    $Error.Clear()
    Try {
        [PSCustomObject]$results = Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI @parameters
    }
    Catch {
        [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
        Write-Warning -Message "Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI failed to execute [$command] with parameters $parameters_display due to [$Message]."
        Break
    }
    [int32]$response_code = $results.response.status
    If ($response_code -ne 0) {
        [string]$full_response_display = $results.response | ConvertTo-Json -Compress -Depth 100
        Write-Warning -Message "The response code was not 0 but was [$response_code]. Body: $full_response_display"
        Break
    }
    $Error.Clear()
    Try {
        [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate = $results.response.data | Select-Object -First 1
    }
    Catch {
        [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
        Write-Warning -Message "Failed to create [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object due to [$Message]."
        Break
    }
    If ($ServiceManagerTemplate.id.Length -eq 0) {
        Write-Warning -Message "The newly created [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] is empty!"
        Break
    }
    $Error.Clear()
    Try {
        [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate = Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id $Id
    }
    Catch {
        [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
        Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate failed to confirm that the [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object [$Id] was created due to [$Message]."
        Break
    }
    If ($Quiet -ne $true) {
        Return $ServiceManagerTemplate
    }
}

Function Remove-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Removes a ServiceManager Template from an AutomateNOW! instance

    .DESCRIPTION
    Removes a ServiceManager Template from an AutomateNOW! instance

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerTemplate
    An [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object representing the ServiceManager Template to be deleted.

    .PARAMETER Force
    Force the removal without confirmation. This is equivalent to -Confirm:$false

    .INPUTS
    ONLY [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects are accepted (including from the pipeline)

    .OUTPUTS
    No success-stream object. A numeric-zero acknowledgment is reported with Write-Verbose. Refusal, diagnostics or uncertain acknowledgment stop subsequent pipeline removals without retry or automatic reference deletion.

    .EXAMPLE
    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManager01' | Remove-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    .EXAMPLE
    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManager01', 'ServiceManager02' | Remove-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    .EXAMPLE
    @( 'ServiceManager1', 'ServiceManager2', 'ServiceManager3') | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate | Remove-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    .EXAMPLE
    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate | ? { $_.ServiceManagerType -eq 'BROADCAST' } | Remove-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    .NOTES
    You must use Connect-AutomateNOW to establish the token by way of global variable.

    #>
    [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess, ConfirmImpact = 'High')]
    Param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false, ValueFromPipeline = $True)]
        [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Force
    )
    Begin {
        $batchStopped = $false
        if (-not (Test-ANOWB3Session)) {
            $batchStopped = $true
            Write-Warning 'A valid session was not confirmed without diagnostics. No template removals were submitted.'
        }
        [string]$command = '/processingTemplate/delete'
        [hashtable]$parameters = @{
            Command = $command
            Method = 'POST'
            ContentType = 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=UTF-8'
        }
        if ($anow_session.NotSecure -eq $true) { $parameters.NotSecure = $true }
    }
    Process {
        if ($batchStopped) { return }
        If ($_.id.Length -gt 0) {
            [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate = $_
        }
        [string]$ServiceManagerTemplate_id = $ServiceManagerTemplate.id
        if ($ServiceManagerTemplate_id.Length -eq 0) {
            $batchStopped = $true
            Write-Warning 'An object with an empty Id was passed to this function. Subsequent removals are stopped.'
            return
        }
        If (($Force -eq $true -and -not $WhatIfPreference) -or ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess("$($ServiceManagerTemplate_id)")) -eq $true) {
            $prepared = Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command New-ANOWTemplateRemovalBody) -OperationParameters @{
                Template = $ServiceManagerTemplate
                ComponentId = 'ProcessingTemplateList'
            }
            if (-not $prepared.Succeeded -or $prepared.Data.Count -ne 1 -or
                $prepared.Data[0] -isnot [string] -or [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($prepared.Data[0])) {
                $batchStopped = $true
                Write-Warning 'ServiceManager template removal preparation failed or emitted a diagnostic. No request was submitted for this input; subsequent removals are stopped.'
                return
            }
            $parameters.Body = $prepared.Data[0]
            $request = Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI) -OperationParameters $parameters
            if (-not $request.Succeeded) {
                $batchStopped = $true
                Write-Warning 'ServiceManager template removal failed or emitted a diagnostic. Its server-side outcome may be uncertain; subsequent removals are stopped and no request is retried.'
                return
            }
            $results = if ($request.Data.Count -eq 1) { $request.Data[0] } else { $null }
            if (-not (Test-ANOWB2Response -Envelopes $request.Data -AcknowledgmentOnly)) {
                $batchStopped = $true
                if ($null -ne $results -and $results.response.data -is [string] -and
                    $results.response.data -match 'Object may still be in use') {
                    Write-Warning 'ServiceManager template is still in use and cannot be removed. Use Find-AutomateNOWObjectReferral to inspect its references. Subsequent removals are stopped; no references were removed.'
                }
                else {
                    Write-Warning 'ServiceManager template removal did not return one numeric-zero acknowledgment. Its server-side outcome may be uncertain; subsequent removals are stopped and no request is retried.'
                }
                return
            }
            Write-Verbose -Message "ServiceManager $ServiceManagerTemplate_id successfully removed"
        }
    }
    End {
    }
}

Function Copy-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Copies a ServiceManager Template from an AutomateNOW! instance

    .DESCRIPTION
    Copies a ServiceManager Template from an AutomateNOW! instance. AutomateNOW object id can never be changed, but we can copy the object to a new id and it will include all of the items therein.

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerTemplate
    Mandatory [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object to be copied.

    .PARAMETER NewId
    Mandatory string indicating the new id or name of the ServiceManager Template. The Id is the same as a primary key, it must be unique. The console will provide the old Id + '_COPY' in the UI when making a copy. The Id is limited to 1024 characters.

    .PARAMETER Description
    Optional description of the ServiceManager Template (may not exceed 255 characters). You may send an empty string here to ensure that the description is blanked out. Do not use this parameter if your intention is to keep the description from the previous ServiceManager Template.

    .PARAMETER UnsetDescription
    Optional switch that will ensure that the newly created ServiceManager Template will not carry over its previous description.

    .PARAMETER Tags
    Optional string array containing the CASE-SENSITIVE id's of the tags to assign to the new ServiceManager Template. The UnsetTags DOES NOT influence this parameter.

    .PARAMETER UnsetTags
    Optional switch that will purposely omit the previously existing tags on the new copy of the ServiceManager Template. You can still specify new tags with -Tags but the old previous ones will not be carried over. In the UI, this is accomplished by clicking the existing tags off.

    .PARAMETER Folder
    Optional name of the folder to place the ServiceManager Template into. The UnsetFolder parameter overrides this setting.

    .PARAMETER UnsetFolder
    Optional switch that will ensure that the newly created ServiceManager Template will not be placed in a folder.

    .PARAMETER Force
    Force the copy without confirmation. This is equivalent to -Confirm:$false

    .PARAMETER Quiet
    Optional switch to suppress the return of the newly created object.

    .INPUTS
    ONLY [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects are accepted. Pipeline support is intentionally unavailable.

    .OUTPUTS
    A verified [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] is returned after acknowledgment, exact destination identity and strict conversion. Quiet suppresses this object while retaining validation.

    .EXAMPLE
    This is a safe standard example that is recommended

    $ServiceManager01 = Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'old_name_ServiceManager01'
    Copy-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate $ServiceManager01 -NewId 'new_name_ServiceManager02'

    .EXAMPLE
    This is a one-liner approach

    Copy-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate (Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'old_name_ServiceManager01') -NewId 'new_name_ServiceManager02'

    .EXAMPLE
    This approach users a For Each loop to iterate through a standard renaming pattern. This approach is not recommended.

    @( 'ServiceManager1', 'ServiceManager2', 'ServiceManager3') | Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate | ForEachObject { Copy-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate $_ -NewId ($_.simpleId -replace 'ServiceManager[0-9]', ()'ServiceManager-' + $_.simpleId[-1]))}

    .NOTES
    Collision, tag, preparation and request diagnostics stop the copy without retry. After dispatch, an unverified result is uncertain and a destination may already exist. Explicitly empty Description is sent as empty; omission retains the source description. Inherited tags are preserved literally unless UnsetTags is selected.

    You must use Connect-AutomateNOW to establish the token by way of global variable.

    The new id (name) of the ServiceManager Template must be unique (per domain). It may consist only of letters, numbers, underscore, dot or hyphen.
    #>
    [OutputType([ANOWServiceManagerTemplate])]
    [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess, ConfirmImpact = 'High')]
    Param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
        [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
        [ValidateScript({ $_ -match '^[0-9a-zA-Z_.-]{1,1024}$' })]
        [string]$NewId,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ValidateScript({ $_.Length -le 255 })]
        [string]$Description,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetDescription,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string[]]$Tags,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetTags,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$Folder,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$UnsetFolder,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Force,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Quiet
    )
    Begin {
        $batchStopped = $false
        $copyContext = $null
        if (-not (Test-ANOWB3Session)) {
            $batchStopped = $true
            Write-Warning 'Template copy session validation failed or emitted a diagnostic. No request was submitted; the copy was stopped.'
        }
    }
    Process {
        if ($batchStopped) { return }
        if (($Force -eq $true -and -not $WhatIfPreference) -or ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess("Copy '$($ServiceManagerTemplate.id)' to '$NewId'")) -eq $true) {
            $checked = Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command Get-ANOWTemplateCopyContext) -OperationParameters @{Kind='ServiceManager';Source=$ServiceManagerTemplate;NewId=$NewId}
            if (-not $checked.Succeeded -or $checked.Data.Count -ne 1) {
                $batchStopped = $true
                Write-Warning 'Template copy source or collision check failed or emitted a diagnostic. No request was submitted; the copy was stopped.'
                return
            }
            $copyContext = $checked.Data[0]
            $options = @{};foreach ($key in $PSBoundParameters.Keys) { $options[$key]=$PSBoundParameters[$key] }
            $prepared = Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command New-ANOWTemplateCopyBody) -OperationParameters @{Context=$copyContext;Options=$options}
            if (-not $prepared.Succeeded -or $prepared.Data.Count -ne 1 -or $prepared.Data[0] -isnot [string]) {
                $batchStopped = $true
                Write-Warning 'Template copy preparation failed or emitted a diagnostic. No request was submitted; the copy was stopped.'
                return
            }
            $parameters = @{Command='/processingTemplate/copy';Method='POST';ContentType='application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=UTF-8';Body=$prepared.Data[0]}
            if ($anow_session.NotSecure -eq $true) { $parameters.NotSecure=$true }
            $sent = Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI) -OperationParameters $parameters
            $verified = if ($sent.Succeeded) { Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command ConvertFrom-ANOWTemplateCopyResponse) -OperationParameters @{Envelopes=$sent.Data;Context=$copyContext} } else { $null }
            if ($null -eq $verified -or -not $verified.Succeeded -or $verified.Data.Count -ne 1) {
                $batchStopped = $true
                Write-Warning 'Template copy acknowledgment or output was not verified. The outcome is uncertain and a destination may already have been created; do not repeat the request. The copy was stopped.'
                return
            }
            Write-Verbose "ServiceManager Template '$NewId' was successfully copied"
            if (-not $Quiet) { $verified.Data[0] }
        }
    }
    End {}
}

Function Rename-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Renames a ServiceManager Template from an AutomateNOW! instance

    .DESCRIPTION
    Performs a pseudo-rename operation of a ServiceManager Template from an AutomateNOW! instance by copying it first and then deleting the source. This function merely combines Copy-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate and Remove-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate therefore it is to be considered destructive.

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerTemplate
    An [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object representing the ServiceManager Template to be renamed.

    .PARAMETER NewId
    Mandatory string indicating the new id or name of the ServiceManager Template. The Id is the same as a primary key, it must be unique. The console will provide the old Id + '_COPY' in the UI when making a copy. The Id is limited to 1024 characters.

    .PARAMETER Force
    Force the renaming without confirmation. This is equivalent to -Confirm:$false

    .PARAMETER Quiet
    Optional switch to suppress the return of the newly renamed object.

    .INPUTS
    ONLY [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects are accepted. There is intentionally no support for the pipeline.

    .OUTPUTS
    The newly renamed [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object will be returned.

    .EXAMPLE
    $ServiceManager_template = Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManager01'
    Rename-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate $ServiceManager_template -NewId 'ServiceManager_TEMPLATE_01'

    .EXAMPLE
    Rename-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate (Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManager01') -NewId 'ServiceManager_TEMPLATE_01'

    .NOTES
    You must use Connect-AutomateNOW to establish the token by way of global variable.

    When renaming, you may only specify a different Id (name).

    This action will be blocked if any existing referrals are found on the object.
    #>
    [OutputType([ANOWServiceManagerTemplate])]
    [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess, ConfirmImpact = 'High')]
    Param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
        [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]
        [ValidateScript({ $_ -match '^[0-9a-zA-Z_.-]{1,1024}$' })]
        [string]$NewId,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Force,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Quiet
    )
    Begin {
        If ((Confirm-AutomateNOWSession -Quiet) -ne $true) {
            Write-Warning -Message "There is not a valid token confirmed."
            Break
        }
        ## Begin standard warning ##
        ## Do not tamper with this below code which makes sure that the object exists before attempting to change it.
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            [boolean]$new_ServiceManager_template_exists = ($null -ne (Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id $NewId))
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate failed to check if the ServiceManager Template [$NewId] already existed due to [$Message]."
            Break
        }
        If ($new_ServiceManager_template_exists -eq $true) {
            [string]$current_domain = $anow_session.header.domain
            Write-Warning -Message "There is already a ServiceManager Template named [$NewId] in [$current_domain]. You may not proceed."
            [boolean]$PermissionToProceed = $false
        }
        [string]$ServiceManagerTemplate_id = $ServiceManagerTemplate.id
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            [boolean]$old_ServiceManager_template_exists = ($null -ne (Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id $ServiceManagerTemplate.simpleId))
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            Write-Warning -Message "Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate failed to check if the ServiceManager Template [$ServiceManagerTemplate_id] already existed due to [$Message]."
            Break
        }
        If ($old_ServiceManager_template_exists -eq $false) {
            [string]$current_domain = $anow_session.header.domain
            Write-Warning -Message "There is not a ServiceManager Template named [$ServiceManagerTemplate_id] in [$current_domain]. You may not proceed."
            [boolean]$PermissionToProceed = $false
        }
        ## End standard warning ##
        ## Begin referrals warning ##
        ## Do not tamper with this below code which makes sure that the object exists before attempting to change it.
        $Error.Clear()
        Try {
            [int32]$referrals_count = Find-AutomateNOWObjectReferral -ServiceManagerTemplate $ServiceManagerTemplate -Sum | Select-Object -Expandproperty referrals
        }
        Catch {
            [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
            Write-Warning -Message "Find-AutomateNOWObjectReferral failed to extract the referrals on ServiceManager Template [$ServiceManagerTemplate_id] due to [$Message]."
            Break
        }
        If ($referrals_count -gt 0) {
            Write-Warning -Message "Unfortunately, you cannot rename a ServiceManager Template that has referrals. This is because the rename is not actually renaming but copying anew and deleting the old. Please, use the Find-AutomateNOWObjectReferral function to identify referrals and remove them."
            Break
        }
        Else {
            Write-Verbose -Message "The ServiceManager Template [$ServiceManagerTemplate_id] does not have any referrals. It is safe to proceed."
        }
    }
    Process {
        If ($PermissionToProceed -ne $false) {
            If (($Force -eq $true -and -not $WhatIfPreference) -or ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess("$($ServiceManagerTemplate_id)")) -eq $true) {
                $Error.Clear()
                Try {
                    [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$new_ServiceManager_template = Copy-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate $ServiceManagerTemplate -NewId $NewId -Force
                }
                Catch {
                    [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
                    Write-Warning -Message "Copy-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate failed to create a new ServiceManager Template [$NewId] as Part 1 of the renaming process due to [$Message]."
                    Break
                }
                If ($new_ServiceManager_template.simpleId -eq $NewId) {
                    Write-Verbose -Message "Part 1: ServiceManager template [$ServiceManagerTemplate_id] successfully copied to [$NewId]"
                }
                Else {
                    Write-Warning -Message "The first phase (Copy-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate) failed."
                    Break
                }
                $Error.Clear()
                Try {
                    Remove-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -ServiceManagerTemplate $ServiceManagerTemplate -Force
                }
                Catch {
                    [string]$Message = $_.Exception.Message
                    Write-Warning -Message "Remove-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate failed to remove [$ServiceManagerTemplate_id] as Part 2 of the renaming process due to [$Message]."
                    Break
                }
                Write-Verbose -Message "Part 2: ServiceManager template [$ServiceManagerTemplate_id] removed"
                Write-Verbose -Message "ServiceManager [$ServiceManagerTemplate_id] successfully renamed to [$NewId]"
                If ($Quiet -ne $true) {
                    Return $new_ServiceManager_template
                }
            }
        }
        Else {
            Write-Warning -Message "No action was taken because either the source object didn't exist or the new object already existed"
        }
    }
    End {
    }
}

Function Start-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate {
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Starts a ServiceManager Template from an AutomateNOW! instance

    .DESCRIPTION
    Starts a ServiceManager Template from an AutomateNOW! instance

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerTemplate
    An [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] object representing the ServiceManager Template to be started.

    .PARAMETER ServiceManagerParameters
    An optional [hashtable] containing the parameters to start the Task Template with. Example: @{"parameter1"="ABC";"parameter2"="123";}

    .PARAMETER Synchronous
    Uses the /executeProcessingSync endpoint instead of /executeNow. This will cause the observer/trigger tasks to be skipped altogether and the actual processing object will be returned. This is ideal for users who have limited privileges.

    .PARAMETER UseAutomaticName
    A switch parameter that is ENABLED BY DEFAULT. You do not need to enable this as it is defaulted to on. This parameter simulates the default format of the executed ServiceManager name (see 'Name' below)

    .PARAMETER Name
    A string representing the name of the running executed ServiceManager. Only use this if you want to OVERRIDE the default naming standard that the console suggests when executing a ServiceManager. The console defaults to a format of "Manual Execution - [ServiceManager name] - [date utc]".

    .PARAMETER Description
    Optional description of the executed ServiceManager (may not exceed 255 characters).

    .PARAMETER Tags
    Optional string array containing the CASE-SENSITIVE id's of the tags to assign to the new ServiceManager.

    .PARAMETER Folder
    Optional name of the folder to place the executed Service Manager into.

    .PARAMETER ProcessingTimestamp
    Optional processing timestamp. You should not use this unless you really need to. Leave this blank for the value to be populated automatically (same as the UI). The format is a UTC datestamp string: 2029-12-31T23:59:59.999

    .PARAMETER DelayedStartTime
    Optional string that allows processing items to start on a specific date or time or delay the execution for a period ranging from days to seconds. Example 1: 2029-12-31, Example 2: 2029-12-31 23:59:59, Example 3: 23:59:59

    .PARAMETER TimeZone
    Optional [ANOWTimeZone] object that modifies (it is unknown exactly what this property modifies since it is not defined in the documentation yet)

    .PARAMETER Priority
    Optional integer between 0 and 1000 to specify the priority of the executed ServiceManager. Defaults to 0.

    .PARAMETER Hold
    Optional switch to set the 'On Hold' property of the executed ServiceManager to enabled. This is $false by default but in the console the checkbox is enabled.

    .PARAMETER VerboseMode
    Optional switch that will cause the Processing Template to "produce more events with minor performance impact"

    .PARAMETER ForceLoad
    Optional switch that overrides any 'Ignore Condition' that might exist on the ServiceManager Template

    .PARAMETER Quiet
    Switch parameter to silence the newly created [ANOWServiceManager] object

    .INPUTS
    ONLY [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate] objects are accepted (including from the pipeline)

    .OUTPUTS
    An [ANOWServiceManager] object representing the started ServiceManager will be returned.

    .EXAMPLE
    Starts a ServiceManager Template named 'ServiceManagerTemplate1'

    Get-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate -Id 'ServiceManagerTemplate1' | Start-AutomateNOWServiceManagerTemplate

    Supplied execution options are preserved per input. A warning or uncertain outcome stops later pipeline inputs; do not repeat an uncertain start. Quiet still validates the strict typed response.

    .NOTES
    You must use Connect-AutomateNOW to establish the token by way of global variable.

    Avoid using the -Name parameter unless you really need to use it. If -Name is not supplied, the parameter set will use -UseAutomaticName (Boolean, default true) instead, which simulates the behavior of the console.

    As of Patch 88, there is a bug where the Folder is not recognized (included) when executing a Service Manager Template.

    #>
    [OutputType([ANOWServiceManager])]
    [CmdletBinding(DefaultParameterSetName = 'UseAutomaticName')]
    Param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ValueFromPipeline = $True)]
        [ANOWServiceManagerTemplate]$ServiceManagerTemplate,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [hashtable]$ServiceManagerParameters,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Synchronous,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false, ParameterSetName = 'UseAutomaticName')]
        [boolean]$UseAutomaticName = $true,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $true, ParameterSetName = 'SpecifyNameManually')]
        [string]$Name,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false, HelpMessage = "Enter a descriptive string up to 255 characters (UTF8 compatible)")]
        [ValidateScript({ $_.Length -le 255 })]
        [AllowEmptyString()]
        [string]$Description,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string[]]$Tags,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$Folder = '',
        [ValidateScript({ $_ -match '^20[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}\.[0-9]{3}$' })]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$ProcessingTimestamp,
        [ValidateScript({ $_ -match '([0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}){0,}( {0,}[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}){0,}' })]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [string]$DelayedStartTime,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [ANOWTimeZone]$TimeZone,
        [ValidateRange(0, 1000)]
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [int32]$Priority = 0,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Hold,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$VerboseMode,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$ForceLoad,
        [Parameter(Mandatory = $false)]
        [switch]$Quiet
    )
    Begin { $batchStopped = $false }
    Process {
        if ($batchStopped) { return }
        $arguments = @{}
        foreach ($key in $PSBoundParameters.Keys) { $arguments[$key] = $PSBoundParameters[$key] }
        $arguments['ServiceManagerTemplate'] = $ServiceManagerTemplate
        $prepared = Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command New-ANOWTemplateStartRequest) -OperationParameters @{Family='ServiceManager';Arguments=$arguments}
        if (-not $prepared.Succeeded -or @($prepared.Data).Count -ne 1 -or $prepared.Data[0] -isnot [hashtable]) {
            $batchStopped = $true
            Write-Warning 'Start preparation was not verified. No start was submitted; later pipeline inputs were stopped.'
            return
        }
        $sent = Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command Invoke-AutomateNOWAPI) -OperationParameters $prepared.Data[0]
        if (-not $sent.Succeeded -or -not (Test-ANOWB2Response -Envelopes $sent.Data)) {
            $batchStopped = $true
            Write-Warning 'The start outcome is uncertain. A run may already exist; do not repeat the start. Later pipeline inputs were stopped.'
            return
        }
        $converted = Invoke-ANOWPrivateCommand -OperationCommand (Get-Command ConvertTo-ANOWB2Result) -OperationParameters @{
            InputObject=@($sent.Data[0].response.data)[0];Family='ServiceManager';Synchronous=($arguments.Synchronous -eq $true)
        }
        if (-not $converted.Succeeded -or @($converted.Data).Count -ne 1 -or -not $converted.Data[0].Success) {
            $batchStopped = $true
            $runNote = ''
            if ($converted.Succeeded -and @($converted.Data).Count -eq 1 -and $converted.Data[0].RunId -is [long]) { $runNote = ' Run ID: ' + $converted.Data[0].RunId + '.' }
            Write-Warning ('The start result could not be represented by the loaded class.' + $runNote + ' A run may already exist; do not repeat the start. Later pipeline inputs were stopped.')
            return
        }
        Write-Verbose 'The start response and typed result were verified.'
        if (-not $Quiet) { $converted.Data[0].Value }
    }
}

